WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.650
Okay. So we have to spend some time today
talking about the general election in the

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.130
United Kingdom late last year, last week

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:11.469
because there is so much being said about
it and how it does or doesn't relate to the

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:16.789
upcoming 2020 election here in the United
States and Donald Trump and Bernie Sanders.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.080
And there's a lot of interesting and good
thoughtful takes about this, but there's also

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.800
some bad talking points and misinformation
that's being spread. So let's start with the

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:32.439
facts. What happened in the UK? Trump Aeon,
conservative party, prime minister Boris Johnson

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:38.969
won with the Tories, the right wing party,
getting a majority of 80 seats in the house

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:43.700
of commons. This truly is huge and it's especially
huge because the Tories had just lost the

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:51.850
majority back in 2017 and then meanwhile a
crushing defeat for the labor party and its

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:57.780
prime minister candidate then leader who has
since resigned, Jeremy Corbyn major losses,

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.489
ended up with the lowest proportion of seats
since 1935 did the labor party, but a brutal

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:04.489
defeat.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:07.540
I mean that's the only way I can really characterize
it. In Jeremy Corbyn has resigned as the head

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.200
of the labor party now. Meanwhile, the Scottish
national party won a huge victory in Scotland

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:18.210
winning 48 of 59 seats. That has some interesting
relationships to the Scottish independence

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:23.370
movement, the Brexit and the view of Brexit
in Scotland, and there's a lot to discuss

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:28.600
there as well. So let's go through it in pieces.
Was this a landslide for the right in the

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:35.590
United Kingdom? It was, absolutely. Is it
a crushing defeat for labor considering that

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:41.170
it is sort of the closest to the modern American
progressive movement of Bernie Sanders and

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:47.330
Elizabeth Warren? It is absolutely a crushing
defeat for labor in the UK, but this is where

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.439
a lot of the analyses started to start to
go off the rails because when we think further,

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:53.649
there are people saying this is a signal.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:58.810
What happened in the UK is a signal that there
is a rejection of the Bernie Warren ideology

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:06.009
and policy prescriptions happening worldwide
and it signals that someone with Bernie or

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:13.050
Warren's platforms here in the United States
will get crushed in 2020 Trump is going to

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:18.040
win. The Democrats would be very, very wrong
to go with someone like Bernie Sanders or

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.910
Elizabeth Morton because they can't win as
proven by the defeat of labor in the U K this

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:28.070
analysis is too simplistic, so let's try to
flush it out a little bit and look at it more

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:36.200
closely. First of all, the starting point
in the UK is a much stronger social democracy

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.930
then we have here in the United States. When
you look at the institutions that they already

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:45.110
have, for example, the UK already has nationalized
healthcare, the NHS. Now I know that there

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:49.780
are some ideas of Boris Johnson dismantling
it, but the point is they've had it for a

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.780
long time.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:57.980
It is popular. Voting for labor is not how
you might get such a system of nationalized

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:05.050
healthcare. They have it. Similarly on education
in the UK, on other safety nets and so many

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:11.720
other areas. These policies are already part
of British society. So when you realize that

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:18.400
they already have these things, labor, there
is not like Bernie or Warren here because

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:24.420
here the left is trying to get lots of things
for the first time that the U K already has.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.260
So the stakes are very different and therefore,
comparing what happened to labor in the UK

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.980
to a Bernie Warren candidacy or presidency
or nomination on the democratic side here

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:40.070
is not an apt comparison in that way in the
United States. The people offering a lot of

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:45.410
those programs that are already part of British
society are the left most of those running

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.600
in the democratic party. Whereas in the U
K many of these programs have been in place

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.600
for decades.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:57.040
So labor being brutally defeated in the UK,
which they were, doesn't confirm that the

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:03.830
policy of Bernie Warren social Democrats is
doomed to fail in the United States. Now,

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:10.690
that gets us to labor as a specific group
of people. Jeremy Corbyn as a person versus

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:18.840
Bernie Warren, et cetera. Having a candidate
who was dogged by allegations of coddling

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:24.870
antisemitism, not taking it seriously, having
unsavory characters in their coalition and

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:31.540
who was seen as flacid in his responses was
not good. Now, we don't need to argue about

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.620
each claim related to antisemitism because
I know there are people who say, no, look,

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.030
he did this investigation into this antisemitic
allegation. We don't need to argue about it.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.980
I don't want to make this an adjudication
of each claim. You can research it for yourself

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:50.340
without adjudicating each claim. I think we
would all agree that the allegations clouded

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:57.380
labor for a long time and they were not definitively
done away with in the eyes of the voters.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.300
And then further, by the way, right after
this election, former London mayor Ken Livingstone,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:06.010
who's a former labor party MP who was actually
suspended over antisemitism, came out and

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:11.770
said, I told you labor loss because of the
unhelpful Jewish vote, which is not only insane,

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:16.330
it's also mathematically impossible. There
are roughly 400,000 Jews in the U K that includes

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.390
children. That includes, you know, that that's
everybody and Corbyn lost the popular vote

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.220
by nearly 4 million votes. So I don't even
know why I have to mention that, but obviously

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.280
those types of claims are absurd, but they're
exactly the type of stuff that people are

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:35.140
concerned about. Labor had a cloud over it
that is specific to labor. That being said,

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:40.010
I have pointed out that Bernie's got some
problematic surrogates. Linda Sarsour is one

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:44.790
also dogged with antisemitism in her past.
I think Bernie should separate from her. I

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.980
just don't know that that is going to take
Bernie down.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:52.840
Uh, this narrative has not become a predominant
one in the United States. Elizabeth Warren

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:58.020
had a racist, homophobic, trans black woman
as a surrogate. We called her out. I believe

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.620
she has been removed from the Warren campaign.
But what's not being met mentioned in all

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.380
of this is Brexit, which is looming over everything
in the U K in a way that it is not here in

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:12.160
the United States. So in addition to the stakes
being different because of the social programs

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:18.080
that the UK already has, in addition to the
cloud over Corbyn being very different than

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:23.370
anything affecting Bernie or Warren right
now, uh, labor's position on Brexit amounted

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:28.080
to maybe, okay, which is a very weak position
and probably didn't help them. So what can

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.040
we glean from the UK results? We can't say
Bernie Warren type politicians are dead in

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.780
the water because they're not, we can't say
Americans don't want progressive policy on

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.389
healthcare and education and corporate reform
because by and large, the polls tell us that

00:06:42.389 --> 00:06:43.389
they do.

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:47.130
What we do need to say is what I've been saying
for a year. No matter what the hypothetical

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:52.350
match-ups might say, Trump might absolutely
crush everyone and we need to fight for every

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:57.150
single vote. No constituency can be assumed
to be with us until they go out and vote in

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:03.050
2020 we can confirm that having a policy and
a set of ideas is vastly more important than

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:08.660
a grievance candidate or an anti Trump candidacy.
That I think is a lesson. It was a right wing

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.800
landslide in the UK, but it's a cautionary
tale about the 2020 election not assigned

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:18.690
to throw in the towel because Bernie Warren
types are obviously being rejected, different

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:23.840
situation, different electorate, different
status quo and starting point. And the answer

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:29.710
to it all is the same thing that we knew before
the UK election, which is get out the vote,

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:34.660
assume nothing and we will actually have some
interesting polling later that confirms that

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.780
all is not well so to speak.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.660
Uh, but more on that coming up a little bit
later

